```php
$x = 5;
$f = function () use ($x) { return $x; };
$x = 7;
echo $f();
```

In PHP, when you use `use ($x)` in a closure, it captures the value of `$x` at the time the closure is defined (by value, not by reference). So when the closure is created, `$x` is 5, and that value is captured. Changing `$x` to 7 after the closure is defined doesn't affect the captured value.

So `$f()` will return 5.

